Jesssica wrote:
> Is it better to delve as deep into the dungeon as possible, going
> downstairs whenever you find a staircase, or to explore every level
> before going down further?

Remember that everything in Nethack has advantages and disadvantages.
The best course to take always depends on your condition currently, and
in
nethack there is never a single best course, because the RNG is always
there
to f*** it all up.

There are advantages and disadvantages to both methods.
1) Exploring each level fully.
advantages
a) You can find all items available on the level
b) You can kill all monsters on the level and leave it relatively empty
for next returns.
disadvantages
a) You can run out of food if you spend too much time on one level.
b) You can gain too many experience levels on a lower level.
You could use your pet though, to prevent this from happening.

2) Descending as soon as you find a staircase
advantages
a) You will find more monsters immediately, good for food.
b) You will get stronger monsters which will provide more experience.
disadvantages
a) You will find stronger monsters than you can handle.
b) You might have left some very important things on previous levels.

If you want to do protection racket, you will want to descend a few
normal
dungeons exploring slowly till your pet becomes strong. Going upto
level 6
is good. And then head for the mines. In the mines descend as soon as
you
find staircase. It is recommended that you have at least 25HP before
you
go into mines, and your pet is the large variety.

Otherwise it makes sense to complete Sokoban first, you could get two
large
pets in the meantime. Sokoban also provides plenty of food. It is
possible to
do the protection racket later by keeping your level low about 5-7. It
would not
be possible to reach Minetown after sokoban below 5, because you will
need
to get rid of the two giant mimics in the last level of Sokoban, which
will get you
above 5.

The only important strategy is to gain levels slowly, till you have an
AC of -10.
Actually if you only kill the newts, eyes, and mimics you will do quite
well.
Let everything else be killed by your pet. If you don't have poison
resistance
it will be better to kill the cave spiders yourself also. Mimics are
easy to kill
if you melee them carefully, but your pet is not intelligent enough to
do that.
This is the reason it is necessary to kill the mimics yourself if your
pet attacks it.
Newts give you mana, which makes them useful to kill. Eyes are also
dangerous
because they make your pet useless by freezing them, and you can kill
them quite
easily by throwing items at them.

